# Default: the maintainers team owns everything
* @thallium-suite/maintainers

# Sensitive paths — require maintainer review.
# Each of these is gated behind review by AGENTS.md: the release and signing
# gates, the build recipe, the image build scripts, and the GNOME factory
# whose buildroot ABI every published RPM is attributable to.
.github/workflows/  @thallium-suite/maintainers
Justfile            @thallium-suite/maintainers
build_scripts/      @thallium-suite/maintainers
factory/            @thallium-suite/maintainers
.packit.yaml        @thallium-suite/maintainers

# Exempt from CODEOWNERS review (Renovate-managed, auto-merged by
# renovate-automerge.yml)
image-versions.yaml

# Enforcement note — read this before requiring a code-owner review.
# GitHub does not let a code-owner review be satisfied by the PR author.
# @thallium-suite/maintainers currently has a single member, so *requiring*
# one would leave every PR permanently unmergeable with no way to approve it.
# The testing ruleset therefore leaves require_code_owner_review in "evaluate"
# (advisory) and the main ruleset does not set it at all. Both are correct
# today and neither blocks anyone. Add MD-2016 or TheOddCell to
# @thallium-suite/maintainers *before* switching testing to "active".